<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bir Hakeim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bir Hakeim was fought in the Libyan desert from 26 May to 11 June 1942, as part of the Battle of Gazala. A Free French brigade under General Marie-Pierre Koenig held the desert fort against German and Italian forces under Erwin Rommel for over two weeks before breaking out. The defence delayed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> advance and gave Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> its first major feat of arms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bir-hakeim.jpg" alt="Battle of Bir Hakeim" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Len Chetwyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Free_French_Foreign_Legionnairs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
